                    briefing_title_r1:      `Round 1 — Diagnose vulnerabilities across six domains`,
                    briefing_text_r1:       `You have the incident report, a multi-domain risk register, the WMS architecture, the supplier-dependency map, the cash-headroom analysis, a fatigue survey and a cyber-posture assessment. Map vulnerabilities across <strong>operational, financial, supply-chain, people, cyber and culture</strong>, then do the hard part: distinguish the two-to-three <strong>could-kill-us</strong> threats from the merely costly. The 48-hour WMS outage with no tested failover is the one that already halted three sites. The trap is <em>declaring everything equally urgent</em> — fourteen red items and a budget that funds maybe five — and ignoring the cultural root cause: a decade of prizing efficiency over adaptability.`,
                    briefing_title_r2:      `Round 2 — Rate the evidence behind every intervention`,
