                    insight_resilient:      `Board-ready resilience: you fixed the could-kill-us gaps first, funded on evidence rather than fashion, and held a genuine balance between defensive robustness and progressive adaptive capacity. This is a plan the board can defend — and it is different from the risk management they have always funded.`,
                    insight_gapopen:        `You left the existential WMS single point of failure unfunded. However much adaptive capacity you bought, the next failed update halts three sites again — and the board will not accept a plan that leaves the could-kill-us gap open. Resilience caps out until that hole is patched.`,
                    insight_overbudget:     `You blew the hard £6M cap — most likely by funding the fashionable AI platform on weak evidence. The board set the cap precisely so that prioritisation, not wish-list breadth, would drive the plan. Exceeding it is the opposite of the discipline they asked for.`,
                    insight_unbalanced:     `You hit the target but the portfolio is lopsided. Over-weighting one side of the defensive/progressive balance creates a new fragility — robustness against yesterday with no adaptability for tomorrow, or vice versa. True resilience holds both.`,
                    insight_short:          `You fell short of the board's resilience target. Re-examine which existential gaps you left unaddressed and whether you funded on evidence or on what sounded good — that is where the score was lost.`,
                    insight_alldefence:     `All-defence portfolio: high robustness, thin adaptive capacity. You are protected against the last disruption and exposed to the next, unnamed one — a demand collapse, a new client model, a regulatory shift.`,
                    insight_allprogress:    `All-progression portfolio: strong adaptive capacity built on thin defensive robustness. Sensing and learning are valuable, but they do not patch an existential single point of failure.`,
